  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThe current implementation introduces a regression for cases where `token_ids` is an iterator or generator (e.g., from a `map` call or a generator expression). The `set(token_ids)` call exhausts the iterator, causing the subsequent list comprehension to iterate over an empty object and return `[]`. Although the docstring specifies 'list form', it is best practice for utility functions to handle iterables robustly, especially since converting to a list has negligible overhead compared to the `tokenizer.decode` calls.\n\n```suggestion\n    token_ids = list(token_ids)\n    unique_ids = set(token_ids)\n    decoded = {}\n    for uid in unique_ids:\n        token_str = tokenizer.decode([uid])\n        decoded[uid] = token_str if token_str is not None else \"\"\n    return [decoded[tid] for tid in token_ids]\n```",
      "created_at": "2026-05-10T06:58:58Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -94,14 +94,12 @@ def convert_ids_list_to_tokens(\n       Python list of token string representations\n \n     \"\"\"\n-    token_str_lst = []\n-    for token_id in token_ids:\n-        # use default skip_special_tokens.\n-        token_str = tokenizer.decode([token_id])\n-        if token_str is None:\n-            token_str = \"\"\n-        token_str_lst.append(token_str)\n-    return token_str_lst\n+    unique_ids = set(token_ids)\n+    decoded = {}\n+    for uid in unique_ids:\n+        token_str = tokenizer.decode([uid])\n+        decoded[uid] = token_str if token_str is not None else \"\"\n+    return [decoded[tid] for tid in token_ids]",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/42211#discussion_r3214466099",
      "id": 3214466099,
